[skineditor]

Skin editor

The skin editor changes the colors and the frame characters of a skin
from inside mc and shows the result as it goes.

Starting it:

  F9 -> Command -> Skin editor...
  F9 -> Command -> Plugin panel... -> Skin editor
  Manage Plugins -> Skin editor -> Enter

It opens on the skin mc runs with.  Skin: [ name ] at the top of the
list opens another one.

The screen:

  The left half lists every key of the skin, grouped by the part of the
  screen it paints: Panels, File types, Dialogs, Menu bar, Editor and so
  on.  The right half is a sample of that part, drawn with the colors of
  the skin as they are now.  Under them: the value of the key under the
  cursor with where each inherited part comes from, and a sentence about
  the key.  A key changed since the last save has a * before it, its
  section too.

  A click on the sample moves the cursor to the key that paints that
  spot; a double click edits it.

Keys in the list:

  Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End   move
  Ctrl-PgUp, Ctrl-PgDn              previous, next section
  Enter, F4                         edit the key
  Space                             show: everything in the sample that
                                    is not this key turns gray, Space
                                    again brings the colors back
  Del                               inherit: the key is removed from
                                    the skin and takes the color of its
                                    section's _default_, or of [core]
  F5                                the value from disk
  Ctrl-U                            undo the last change, however many
                                    times; the cursor goes to its key
  Ctrl-Ins                          copy the three parts of the key
  Shift-Ins                         paste: asks whether to paste all of
                                    it, the foreground, the background
                                    or the attributes; an inherited part
                                    is pasted as inherited
  F2                                save
  F12                               save as
  Esc, F10                          leave; asks first when there are
                                    changes

Every change goes to the screen at once.  Esc puts the skin mc had back.
Save writes the file to your skins directory, ~/.local/share/mc6/skins,
and makes it the skin mc runs with; a skin from the system directory is
saved as a copy there under a name you give, and the copy shadows the
original.

Edit as file, in the button row, opens the skin file in mcedit, for the parts this
dialog does not show, the aliases for one.  Unsaved changes are saved
or dropped first, and the file is read again when the editor closes.

The Color dialog:

  Foreground and background each have a palette of the 16 named colors,
  an Inherit box, a Terminal default box and the buttons 256.. and
  RGB..  256.. opens the 256-color picker: the 16 system colors, the
  6x6x6 cube and the 24 grays; the line under it names the color three
  ways.  RGB.. asks for a #rrggbb value.  The two buttons are off on a
  terminal that cannot show those colors.

  Style has Inherit and the attributes bold, italic, underline, reverse
  and blink.

  The changes show in the sample box, in the pane behind the dialog and
  on the screen as they are made.  Reset puts the value from disk back,
  Cancel the value the dialog opened with.

Characters:

  The sections Frames, Panel marks, Find and editor marks and Spinner
  hold characters, not colors.  Enter asks for the character, or the
  whole string of the spinner; an empty value puts the built-in one
  back.

Notes:

  A key that is not in the skin file inherits: the value line says from
  where.  [core] _default_ is the one key every skin must have; making
  it inherit sets it to the terminal's own colors instead.

  The file is written with its comments and its order kept.  The flags
  256colors and truecolors in [skin] are set from the colors in use.
